   ╭─[ reject/ring-different.sw:5:80 ]
   │
 5 │ theorem extra (b: Nat) (m: Nat) (p: Nat): b * m * p + b = b * m * p + 2 * b := ring
   │                                                                                ──┬─  
   │                                                                                  ╰─── the two sides are different polynomials
   │ 
   │ Note 1: left:  b * m * p + b
   │ 
   │ Note 2: right: b * m * p + 2 * b
   │ 
   │ Note 3: the left side has `b` less
   │ 
   │ Note 4: this statement is false; a counterexample:
   │           b = 1
   │           m = 0
   │           p = 0
   │         `b * m * p + b = b * m * p + (2 * b)` is false:
   │           left:  1
   │           right: 2
